    35	## 1. Reviewed S2 pinning and exact curve data
    36	
    37	Write $D=D_A$ for the unique component with nontrivial meridian.  The
    38	reviewed ownership rows are exactly
    39	
    40	| row | dicritical ownership | component data $(W,a)$ |
    41	|---|---|---|
    42	| P3a | $(\mu,\operatorname{corr},s)=(2,0,1)$ over $D$; one $(1,0,1)$ over each of two other components | $(2,3),(1,4),(1,4)$, $m=3$ |
    43	| P3b | $(2,0,1)$ over $D$; both $(1,0,1)$'s over one other component | $(2,3),(2,3)$, $m=2$ |
    44	
    45	This is `B0:233-244,506-515`, confirmed at `REV:38-56,68-78`.  The
    46	cover-ramification floor forces every displayed $s=1$, not equality by
    47	attainment (`REV:48-54,109-120`).  Consequently every component has
    48	normalization $\mathbb A^1$, one place at infinity, and a birational polynomial
    49	parametrization.  On $D$, zero correction makes the normalization map immersive.
    50	Thus $D$ is irreducible and rational and every affine singularity has exactly
    51	two smooth branches.  If their contact is $k_z\geq1$, the germ is
    52	$A_{2k_z-1}$ and $\delta_z=k_z$; tangency is allowed.
