   314	
   315	### 4.1 Coprime infinity
   316	
   317	If $g=1$, the roots over a large circle satisfy uniformly
   318	$t_j\sim cR^{1/d}e^{i(\theta+2\pi j)/d}$ and their $q$-values have leading
   319	phase $n(\theta+2\pi j)/d$.  Coprimality keeps the leading points separated,
