   539	## 6. Verdict and first missing tool
   540	
   541	**Verdict: S2 remains OPEN, but its entire coprime stratum is KILLED and its
   542	affine-normal-form $(6,4)$ cable stratum is KILLED.**  The same conclusion applies
   543	to both P3a and P3b; their extra components have trivial meridians.  The surviving
   544	question is now
   545	
   546	```text
   547	OPEN[PI1-S5-NODAL-NONCOPRIME]:
   548	  Does there exist an irreducible polynomial curve D, normalization A1 and one
   549	  place at infinity, with a degree-minimal target parametrization in affine
   550	  normal form (3.1), d>n>=1, g=gcd(d,n)>=2, every affine singularity two
   551	  smooth branches of contact k_z,
   552	  M_infinity+2T >= 3d-2, and a surjection pi1(C2-D)->S5 sending meridians to
   553	  transpositions and each local branch pair to disjoint transpositions?
