+\[
+ (8,6,3),\ (8,6,7),\ (8,6,9),\ (8,6,11),\qquad
+ (9,6,2),\ (9,6,4),
+\]
+
+with invariant triples displayed in §3.  The tangential residual is exactly
+the candidate (T)-ranges in §4.  Every complementary ((\Delta,T)) subrow is
+KILLED by N-A-RES.  This is the S2 analogue of a low-degree residual ledger,
+but not an all-degree pin: the charged packet supplies no degree cap
+(`K:82-88`; `R:420-437`).
+
+For every candidate, two nonnumerical gates remain: construct or exclude an
+immersive polynomial representative whose affine fibres have only the stated
+double contacts, and compute its iterated cable action on a generating
+five-letter transposition tuple.  If the latter proves INF-TRIVIAL instead of
+killing the tuple, the next promoted route is the typed quintic-plane OPEN,
+not the N=4 triple-plane theorem (`K:571-583`; `R:423-437`).
