+
+For example, `(9,6,4)` has
+((\delta_\infty,\delta_{\rm aff},M_\infty)=(22,6,25)), so its nodal
+subrow is exactly sharp for `(M-INF)`, consistent with the coordinator's
+description of that numerical candidate as a sharpness witness (`C:59-63`).
+That description is not promoted here into S2 attainment.
+
+The local (S_5) requirement adds no further scalar cull: at every contact the
+two transpositions are disjoint and commute, for every (k_z).  The promoted
+`(6,4)` block-product calculation is special to its three outer two-strand
+tubes and is not extrapolated.  In particular, odd (d=9) only prevents full
