+- The normalization parameter (t), normalization place
+  (widetilde Q_\infty), physical point (P_\infty), affine point (z),
+  pole delta sequence, and cover tuple remain distinct.  Later denominator
+  shedding is not identified with the leading pair.
+- The cluster identity is applied only after the promoted one-place infinity
+  class and after Proposition 2.1 supplies the last maximal-contact value.
+  The coprime formula is never used on a cable.
+- The target ring, coefficient field, generator order, automorphism, inverse,
+  raw remainder, and zero/constant branches are explicit in (2.2).  No
+  `sat()`, quotient normal form, ambiguous prime, or undeclared ring map is
+  used.
+- N-A-RES is used only in its proved implication direction.  A lower bound,
+  numerical equality, delta sequence, or AM converse is never called
+  attainment.
+- No per-ray exit price, merge-free M-descent, (V_{2,a}) endpoint argument,
+  or target/arrival index is used.  Raw coordinate degree and degree-minimal
+  row label are kept separate.  Consequently this report makes no new exit
+  claim and contains no `charge_basis` declaration.
+
+**Verdict.**  The first residual numerical pin is now explicit: after the
+promoted kills and degree-minimal reduction, the low-degree cage begins with
+the `(8,6)` and `(9,6)` tables in §§3--5.  Nodal survivors are the six listed
+rows; tangential survivors are the stated (T)-subrows.  All other subrows
+through (d=9) are killed or are not minimal.  S2 itself, realization of the
+candidate rows, their cable (S_5) test, and every (d\ge10) row remain
+typed OPEN.

